{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>That I may know You, in order that I may find favor.</b> The explanation is: since it is not befitting proper conduct for a servant to say to his master that he wishes to know Him, therefore he determined to say <b>in order that</b>, etc. — meaning, so that there may be straight conduct in constancy before You, and this is the finding of favor that is perceived in the eyes of HaShem." "<b>And see that this nation is Your people.</b> Here Moses spoke in that which is hidden from the eyes of man, and was made known to him, and it is the argument that is heard before the Creator above all the arguments he made — namely, that the souls of Israel are the portion of HaShem, as I explained in the song of Ha'azinu at the verse (Deuteronomy 32:9) ״כִּי חֵלֶק ה׳ עַמּוֹ״, and this is also what HaShem alluded to in saying (Exodus 20:2) ״אָנֹכִי ה׳ אֱלֹהֶיךָ״, as I explained there. And this is what he argued in saying <b>and see</b> — meaning, see this particular point — <b>that this nation is Your people</b>, meaning, they are attached and joined to You, and how could You despise the portion of the Supernal One. Understand this."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:24.196987516Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}